<title>FRANCE: DHL repeats French trucker contingency plan.</title>
<headline>DHL repeats French trucker contingency plan.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>DHL Worldwide Express said it will repeat contingency plans this evening for its road services in response to industrial action by French lorry drivers.</p>
<p>&quot;We have cancelled almost all of our scheduled trucking services between Paris and Brussels because of fears of road blocks and the slack will be taken up by a 20-tonne Boeing 727F which will make two round trips between Brussels and Paris as it did Monday evening, Monday,&quot; a Brussels based DHL official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Elsewhere, DHL's air cargo line-haul services from Brussels to French provincial cities Nantes, Bordeaux, Toulouse, Marseille, Nice and Lyon will operate as normal, the official said. -- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
